  "instance_name": "racial_justification_of_violence",
  "label": "The act of justifying violence based on racial stereotypes or prejudices",
  "description": "Racial justification of violence refers to the act of justifying violence based on racial stereotypes or prejudices, often by implying that the victims are not human or that their killing is not a serious issue. In the meme, the implication that killing zombies (non-human entities) is not homicide is used to justify racially motivated violence. This requires understanding of the concept of racial justification of violence and its role in promoting harmful ideologies.",
